====== Gfg  Subset Sum Problem =======

Step-by-step algorithm for checking if a subset with given sum exists:

Step 1: Create a boolean array `ar` of size `sum + 1`.
This array will store whether a particular sum is possible or not.

Step 2: Set `ar[0] = true`.
This means a sum of 0 is always possible (by choosing no elements).

Step 3: Traverse each element in the given array.

Step 4: For each element, update the boolean array from right to left (from `sum` down to the current element value).

* Sub-step 4a: For each value `j` from `sum` down to `arr[i]`,
  check if the sum `j` can be formed.

* Sub-step 4b: Update
  `ar[j] = ar[j] OR ar[j - arr[i]]`

  This means:

  * If `ar[j]` was already true, keep it true.
  * Otherwise, check if `j - arr[i]` was previously possible.
    If yes, then `j` is also possible by adding the current element.

Step 5: Repeat this process for all elements in the array.

Step 6: After processing all elements, check `ar[sum]`.

Step 7: If `ar[sum]` is true, a subset with the given sum exists.
Otherwise, it does not exist.

Time Complexity:
Outer loop runs n times.
Inner loop runs up to sum times.
Time Complexity = O(n × sum)

Space Complexity:
Boolean array of size `sum + 1` is used.
Space Complexity = O(sum)


     ----------------> Code <-------------------

class Solution {

    static Boolean isSubsetSum(int arr[], int sum) {
        boolean[] ar=new boolean[sum+1];
        ar[0]=true;
        
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            for(int j=sum;j>=arr[i];j--){
                ar[j]=ar[j] || ar[j-arr[i]];
            }
        }
        return ar[sum];
    }
}
